  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROGRESS: Promoting Growth, Resilience, Economic Stability and Sustainability in the Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Growth, Resilience, Economic Stability and Sustainability in the Philippines (PROGRESS) will be Australia&apos;s new flagship inclusive economic growth program in the Philippines. The goal of PROGRESS is to contribute towards a prosperous and economically resilient Philippines. PROGRESS will elevate Australia&apos;s direct engagement on economic cooperation in the Philippines, in support of the Philippine Development Plan (2023-2028), and will directly support development cooperation objectives under the Australia-Philippines Development Partnership Plan 2024-2029 (DPP). 
It will support the Philippines&apos; economy by addressing issues and sectors strategic to the Philippines and Australia, such as enhancements to the business environment, support for targeted economic reforms, and support for the growth of priority sectors  such as clean energy and resources.</narrative>
  </description>
